#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096502 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96967f25-565a-5338-878e-00fd30055772" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area Bounded Below a Curve and Above the X-Axis"}] :question/id #uuid "dc29cf6e-4f68-552e-ae7a-f9834eec1bd7" :question/math-academy-id "e-781" :question/problem "Find the area between the curve $y=x^2-2x+2,$ the $x$-axis, and the lines $x=0$ and $x=2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/assets/6b85f10cde49017eac1c56ad1b8abbcdf3033a367d5e1eb162dd89fbb6141461.png)" :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}({x}^{2}-2x+2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-2{\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\,\\text{d}x+2{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}|}_{0}^{2}-2\\cdot {\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}|}_{0}^{2}+2x{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{8}{3}-0)-2(2-0)+2(2-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}-4+4 \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096503 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ad216da-1bcf-5b87-9436-918ef1e5015a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area Bounded Above a Curve and Below the X-Axis"}] :question/id #uuid "5893a692-573a-5e1a-81aa-db34fa6059ed" :question/math-academy-id "e-782" :question/problem "Find the area of the closed region between the curve $y=x^2-1$ and the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the intersections of the curve with the $x$-axis:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-1 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =1 \\\\ x & =\\pm 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe draw a sketch of the region, as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/assets/9b78aad41f84f6a6997914bd8d4243f30cb0ebea4edb5305962dc11c7a46a807.png)\n\nWe want the area between the curve $y=x^2-1$ and the $x$-axis, from $x=-1$ to $x=1.$ To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}({x}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}|}_{-1}^{1}-x{|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{3}-(-\\frac{1}{3}))-(1-(-1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}-2 \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is $\\dfrac{4}{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186286979 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ad216da-1bcf-5b87-9436-918ef1e5015a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area Bounded Above a Curve and Below the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02d2d42c-a2f6-5794-98d1-e9f45e363f20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286981} {:answer/id #uuid "8aaa62df-b3d3-5788-932b-ac74df33f711" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286982} {:answer/id #uuid "6c04dcf5-bb0e-519d-bea6-29b3eaafd011" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286983} {:answer/id #uuid "8a2f18ac-79ee-5da0-af4b-3b111f5d3115" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286984} {:answer/id #uuid "edb5b488-bf49-5b1d-877c-a110c0b28fc5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286985}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8aaa62df-b3d3-5788-932b-ac74df33f711" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286982} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d637e68-da4f-5b6c-a95a-d87f9ad2692b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286980}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0c21d4e0-baa2-59e6-b265-1bfdd4a8ba84" :question/math-academy-id "q-103824" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/assets/97cf633bce7a8eeef443757e62d52f356c911b6aee3d8019d434d514416b0049.png)\n\nA region is bounded by the curve $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and the $x$-axis between $x=-\\pi $ and $x=0$, as shown above. What is the area of the region?" :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{0}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x{|}_{-\\pi }^{0} \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)-(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\pi )) \\\\  & =-1-(1) \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is $2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186286993 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96967f25-565a-5338-878e-00fd30055772" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area Bounded Below a Curve and Above the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ad04aee-4354-5499-a9c4-5d32782153cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{3}+\\ln(2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286995}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7ad04aee-4354-5499-a9c4-5d32782153cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{3}+\\ln(2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286995} :answer-field/id #uuid "cfbc56d0-6cf5-56e8-832a-e1f5ce426489" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286994}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3dc8a6c1-7592-5eeb-a313-53d3c7edaf54" :question/math-academy-id "q-316022" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/assets/b5432ed129d85a3718f8e5ebe0cca141731c366d1b32e8e72d0916c60c34de2c.png)\n\nA region in the $x$-$y$ plane is bounded by the curve $y={sec}^{2}⁡x+\\frac{1}{x}$, and the $x$-axis between $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ and $x=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$, as shown above. \nFind the area $A$ of the region. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}({sec}^{2}⁡(x)+\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}{sec}^{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,+\\,{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)){|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{3})-(\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{\\pi /3}{\\pi /6} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287002 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96967f25-565a-5338-878e-00fd30055772" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area Bounded Below a Curve and Above the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f2234af5-c4b4-528e-a73d-9112c3bcf211" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287004} {:answer/id #uuid "dd04ae4e-8b2a-583a-99ac-cefd48c3c441" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287005}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd04ae4e-8b2a-583a-99ac-cefd48c3c441" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287005} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a308356-6fe7-5b58-823a-c078c0fdfb17" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287003}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7dc244c3-54c6-5170-b8f9-917b4e9e083b" :question/math-academy-id "q-345322" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/assets/66bf8c1144de1ad65938345d2937fddd6fb43ec4822a2b98a9b5383ca2609567.png)\n\nA region is bounded by the curve $y=-2{x}^{2}+3$ and the $x$-axis between $x=0$ and $x=1$, as shown above. Find the area $A$ of the region. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(-2{x}^{2}+3)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(-2\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+3x){|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(-\\frac{2}{3}+3)-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287006 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ad216da-1bcf-5b87-9436-918ef1e5015a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area Bounded Above a Curve and Below the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e1f9a6a-e10b-58a2-a01b-182ae2eeed8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287008}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e1f9a6a-e10b-58a2-a01b-182ae2eeed8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287008} :answer-field/id #uuid "8715be83-ce41-55ca-9341-52a474fd23f8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287007}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "10fa10cd-fc6f-507a-99f5-6fa17f1da5d9" :question/math-academy-id "q-345343" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/assets/34eb73b6bd93f9a45b666ed0599719a09b54948d1d81b14ceea9b46f99b75054.png)\n\nFind the area between the curve $y=-{x}^{2}-1$, the $x$-axis, and the line $x=-1$ and $x=1$ (shown above). Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}(-{x}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}|}_{-1}^{1}-x{|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =-(\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{(-1)^{3}}{3})-(1-(-1)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}-2 \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is \n\n$$\nA=-{\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{8}{3}.\n$$"}]}
